 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** Linear with respect to the number of chunks generated, $O(N)$ where $N = \text{width} \times \text{height} \times \text{gridSize}^2$ [S1, unofficial].
-- **Memory Complexity:** Proportional to the number of pending chunks in the queue, $O(N)$ [S1, unofficial].
-- **Performance:** The method is lightweight, primarily involving arithmetic operations and queue pushes [S1, unofficial].
-- **Strengths:** Deterministic spiral order ensures predictable loading sequences; separation of generation order from noise evaluation allows flexible sampling strategies [S1, unofficial].
-- **Limitations:** The spiral pattern may not align with cache locality for subsequent noise evaluation if the sampler expects spatial coherence [G].
-- **When to Use:** When progressive loading or mesh generation requires a specific traversal order independent of spatial proximity [S1, unofficial].
-- **When Not to Use:** When spatial locality is more important than traversal order, or when the scene is static and pre-generated [G].
